# `todo/t1077` REGRESSION CELL — payload: RESOURCE-CARRYING ENUM,
# consume shape: WHOLE-VALUE ASSIGN.
#
# This cell's failure face is neither of the two `t1077` was filed on. Reading
# a nested `Box[Box[E]]` into an `E` local did not crash and did not print a
# wrong value — it made the COMPILER panic, before any code was emitted:
#
#   PRE-fix, BOTH lanes: build rc 101
#     Tier 2a consume-site violation: 1 violation(s) ...
#     fn @main bb0 i13 — AssignIntoOwnedSlot(dst: Tag) — untracked source
#     consumed (ownership not decided)
#
# ⚠ THE ENUM MUST CARRY A RESOURCE. A fieldless `enum E: A / B` builds and
# SIGSEGVs at run time instead, which is the ordinary face — so a fixture named
# "enum payload" built on a fieldless enum MISSES this cell entirely (Core #12:
# the NAME is a claim about SCOPE).
#
# EXPECTED OUTPUT: alphabeta
# EXPECTED EXIT: 0 on BOTH backends.
#
# ⛔ Lives in `known_gaps/` with a LIVE test for TWO reasons, and closing only
# the first is not licence to graduate it: (1) the self-host cannot compile any
# nested `Box` at all (`todo/t1311`), and top level is auto-scanned into
# `runtime_parity_corpus`; (2) it LEAKS at scope exit (`todo/t1309`, blocked on
# `todo/t0096`), and top level is also the ASan corpus.

enum Tag:
    Named(String)
    Numbered(int)

void main():
    Box[Box[Tag]] w = Box[Box[Tag]](Box[Tag](Tag.Named("alpha" + "beta")))
    Tag t = (*(*w))
    match t:
        case Named(s):
            print(s)
        case Numbered(n):
            print(n)
